### String and character enhancements

.NET 11 introduces significant enhancements to string and character manipulation APIs, making it easier to work with Unicode characters and runes.

#### Rune support in String methods

The [String](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string) class now includes methods that accept [Rune](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.text.rune) parameters, enabling you to search, replace, and manipulate strings using Unicode scalar values directly. These new methods include:

*   `Contains` - Check if a string contains a specific rune: [String.Contains(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.contains#system-string-contains\(system-text-rune\)) and [String.Contains(Rune, StringComparison)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.contains#system-string-contains\(system-text-rune-system-stringcomparison\)).
*   `StartsWith` and `EndsWith` - Check if a string starts or ends with a specific rune: [String.StartsWith(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.startswith#system-string-startswith\(system-text-rune\)), [String.StartsWith(Rune, StringComparison)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.startswith#system-string-startswith\(system-text-rune-system-stringcomparison\)), [String.EndsWith(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.endswith#system-string-endswith\(system-text-rune\)), and [String.EndsWith(Rune, StringComparison)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.endswith#system-string-endswith\(system-text-rune-system-stringcomparison\)).
*   `IndexOf` and `LastIndexOf` - Find the position of a rune in a string: [String.IndexOf(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.indexof#system-string-indexof\(system-text-rune\)), [String.IndexOf(Rune, StringComparison)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.indexof#system-string-indexof\(system-text-rune-system-stringcomparison\)), [String.LastIndexOf(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.lastindexof#system-string-lastindexof\(system-text-rune\)), and [String.LastIndexOf(Rune, StringComparison)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.lastindexof#system-string-lastindexof\(system-text-rune-system-stringcomparison\)).
*   `Replace` - Replace occurrences of one rune with another: [String.Replace(Rune, Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.replace#system-string-replace\(system-text-rune-system-text-rune\)).
*   `Split` - Split a string using a rune as the separator: [String.Split(Rune, StringSplitOptions)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.split#system-string-split\(system-text-rune-system-stringsplitoptions\)) and [String.Split(Rune, Int32, StringSplitOptions)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.split#system-string-split\(system-text-rune-system-int32-system-stringsplitoptions\)).
*   `Trim`, `TrimStart`, and `TrimEnd` - Trim runes from strings: [String.Trim(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.trim#system-string-trim\(system-text-rune\)), [String.TrimStart(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.trimstart#system-string-trimstart\(system-text-rune\)), and [String.TrimEnd(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.string.trimend#system-string-trimend\(system-text-rune\)).

Many of these methods include overloads that accept a [StringComparison](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.stringcomparison) parameter for culture-aware comparisons.

#### Char.Equals with StringComparison

The [Char](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.char) struct now includes an [Char.Equals(Char, StringComparison)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.char.equals#system-char-equals\(system-char-system-stringcomparison\)) method that accepts a [StringComparison](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.stringcomparison) parameter, allowing you to compare characters using culture-aware or ordinal comparisons.

#### Rune support in TextInfo

The [TextInfo](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.globalization.textinfo) class now provides [TextInfo.ToLower(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.globalization.textinfo.tolower#system-globalization-textinfo-tolower\(system-text-rune\)) and [TextInfo.ToUpper(Rune)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.globalization.textinfo.toupper#system-globalization-textinfo-toupper\(system-text-rune\)) methods that accept [Rune](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.text.rune) parameters, enabling you to perform case conversions on individual Unicode scalar values.

#### StringBuilder.MoveChunks

To transfer content without copying characters, use the new static [StringBuilder.MoveChunks(StringBuilder)](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.text.stringbuilder.movechunks#system-text-stringbuilder-movechunks\(system-text-stringbuilder\)) method, which moves all content from a source `StringBuilder` to a new `StringBuilder`. After the call, the source `StringBuilder` has a length of 0:

```
var source = new StringBuilder("Hello, ");
source.Append("World!");

// MoveChunks transfers all content from source to a new StringBuilder.
// After the call, source contains no characters.
StringBuilder dest = StringBuilder.MoveChunks(source);
Console.WriteLine(dest);          // Hello, World!
Console.WriteLine(source.Length); // 0
```

### Base64 encoding improvements

.NET 11 adds new APIs and overloads to the existing [Base64](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.buffers.text.base64) type, providing comprehensive support for Base64 encoding and decoding. These additions offer improved performance and flexibility compared to existing methods.

#### New Base64 APIs

The new APIs support encoding and decoding operations with various input and output formats:

*   **Encoding to chars**: [EncodeToChars](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.buffers.text.base64.encodetochars) and [EncodeToString](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.buffers.text.base64.encodetostring)
*   **Encoding to UTF-8**: [EncodeToUtf8](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.buffers.text.base64.encodetoutf8)
*   **Decoding from chars**: [DecodeFromChars](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.buffers.text.base64.decodefromchars)
*   **Decoding from UTF-8**: [DecodeFromUtf8](/en-us/dotnet/api/system.buffers.text.base64.decodefromutf8)

These methods provide both high-level convenience methods (that allocate and return arrays or strings) and low-level span-based methods (for zero-allocation scenarios).

